_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 22
---
order: 22
---
short_label: VI.22
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If four straight lines are proportional, then the rectilinear figures similar and similarly described upon them are also proportional; and, if the rectilinear figures similar and similarly described upon them are proportional, then the straight lines are themselves also proportional.
----
proof:

Let the four straight lines {AB}, {CD}, {EF}, and {GH} be proportional, so that {AB} is to {CD} as {EF} is to {GH}.  Let the similar and similarly situated rectilinear figures {KAB} and {LCD} be described on {AB} and {CD}, and the similar and similarly situated rectilinear figures {MF} and {NH} be described on {EF} and {GH}.

I say that {KAB} is to {LCD} as {MF} is to {NH}.

Take a third proportional {O} to {AB} and {CD}, and a third proportional {P} to {EF} and {GH}. [!just VI.11]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="530" height="340" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VI.22 diagram" src="propVI22.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the four given lines AB, CD, EF, GH on one baseline
    // (H derived, so that AB : CD = EF : GH), the similar triangles KAB, LCD
    // and the similar quadrilaterals MF, NH on them (L, N, N1 derived), the
    // third proportionals O and P (O1, P1 derived), and the converse's QR
    // with SR described on it (S, S1 derived). QR is a free pair of sliders,
    // as in Joyce's figure: the reductio's "let EF be to QR as AB to CD" is
    // what the proof goes on to refute, so it is not built to the ratio.
    //
    // The four lines and QR are only polygon sides there. The walk needs
    // them before the figures exist, so ABs, CDs, EFs, GHs, QRs are solid
    // slide twins over those sides, hidden at rest (initiallyHidden); the
    // names AB, CD, EF, GH, QR are transparent targets for captions and
    // prose. The figures are reached by their prose names KAB, LCD, MF, NH,
    // SR, which are faceless twins of Joyce's filled ABK, CDL, EFM, GHN, QRS
    // (a highlighted filled polygon is raised, #140). No angles are marked:
    // the argument is all ratios.
    //
    // The statement stands over the givens and their figures; the
    // converse withdraws O and P, and the close withdraws QR and SR.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): the sliders A-G and the
    // invisible guide ends U0, U1, L0, L1, H1 are givens. K, M, M1 (free)
    // arrive with the figures, O0, P0 (invisible sliders) with O and P,
    // and Q, R only in the converse, so all seven are deferred.
